<h1 class="text-heading font-semibold mb-4">Role Mapping</h1>
<p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
  The value that must appear in the admin group claim of the sign-in token to grant instance-admin access. The claim path itself is
  set by the bootstrap wizard and is not changed here. The value must be in the token of the person who saves it (it is checked against the fresh sign-in this save asks for), otherwise the save is refused.
</p>

<p id="admin-claim-path-line" data-role="admin-claim-path" class="text-sm mb-4">
  <span :if={@claim_path}>Looked up in the claim: <code>{@claim_path}</code></span>
  <span :if={!@claim_path}>
    Looked up in every claim of the token except protocol and identity claims (sub, email, name, typ, acr and similar); no claim path is stored.
  </span>
</p>

<p :if={Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :info)} class="alert alert-success mb-4" role="status">
  {Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :info)}
</p>
<p :if={Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :error)} class="alert alert-error mb-4" role="alert">
  {Phoenix.Flash.get(@flash, :error)}
</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/config/role-mapping" class="max-w-md flex flex-col gap-4">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_click_proof" value="" data-click-proof />
  <div>
    <label for="admin_group_claim" class="block text-sm mb-1">Admin group value</label>
    <input
      id="admin_group_claim"
      name="admin_group_claim"
      value={@value}
      class="input input-bordered w-full"
      aria-describedby={if @error, do: "admin-claim-path-line admin-group-claim-error", else: "admin-claim-path-line"}
      aria-invalid={if @error, do: "true"}
      autofocus={@error != nil}
    />
    <p :if={@error} id="admin-group-claim-error" role="alert" data-field="admin_group_claim" class="text-error text-sm mt-1">
      {@error}
      <a :if={@reauth_link} href={@reauth_link} class="link">Sign in again, then enter the value once more</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p id="role-mapping-lockout-hint" class="alert alert-warning text-sm">
    This value decides who is an administrator. A wrong value locks all administrators out at their next sign-in or session refresh, and an
    open session cannot undo it: the correction needs the operator (bin/nebu rpc on the server, or database access; deployment guide, "Admin configuration forms and
    their protection"). The save is refused when your own fresh sign-in does not hold the value, and other administrators lose access when their token lacks it.
    A value that is too BROAD is as dangerous: it makes every user an administrator. Use a group that only administrators have. If the bootstrap wizard stored no claim path, the admin check scans ALL claims of the token,
    so a value that appears anywhere in every token grants admin to everybody.
  </p>
  <p id="role-mapping-reauth-hint" class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
    Saving this setting needs a fresh sign-in. If you are asked to sign in again, you return to this page and must enter your change again.
  </p>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary self-start" aria-describedby="role-mapping-lockout-hint role-mapping-reauth-hint">Save</button>
</form>
